  "tutorialHelpTooltip": "Application guide and tutorial",
  "tutorialWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to SoilScope!",
  "tutorialWelcomeDesc": "SoilScope is a scientific Soil-Plant-Atmosphere Continuum (SPAC) simulator. In this tutorial we introduce the key controls and views so you can manage the simulation and interpret biophysical processes effortlessly.",
  "tutorialWelcomePoint1": "Shoot growth directly reflects root water and nutrient uptake capacity.",
  "tutorialWelcomePoint2": "Water and ions migrate through the soil according to physical laws (Richards equation).",
  "tutorialWelcomePoint3": "Soil microbes and mycorrhizal fungi convert organic matter into plant-available nutrients.",
  "tutorialCanvasTitle": "Simulation Canvas & Inspection Points",
  "tutorialCanvasDesc": "In the main view you observe a 2D physical world: shoot and root development, soil strata, and dynamic nutrient particle fluxes.",
  "tutorialCanvasPoint1": "Click on glowing hotspots on soil and plant to launch microscopic cross-sectional analysis.",
  "tutorialCanvasPoint2": "Hover over any component to inspect real-time scientific telemetry and chemical equations.",
  "tutorialDashboardTitle": "HUD Dashboard & Soil Profile",
  "tutorialDashboardDesc": "The left dashboard allows deep biophysical and biochemical inspection across all soil layers.",
  "tutorialDashboardPoint1": "Monitor layer-by-layer moisture (θ), temperature, pH, redox potential, and electrical conductivity.",
  "tutorialDashboardPoint2": "Soil Texture Triangle illustrates relative proportions of clay, silt, and sand.",
  "tutorialDashboardPoint3": "Track MAOM and POM organic carbon pools and microbial biomass dynamics.",
  "tutorialControlsTitle": "Control Panel & Interventions",
  "tutorialControlsDesc": "Use the right control panel to adjust atmospheric drivers and apply agricultural management.",
  "tutorialControlsPoint1": "Adjust weather: photosynthetic solar radiation (PAR), precipitation, air temperature, and CO₂.",
  "tutorialControlsPoint2": "Interventions: irrigation, mineral or organic fertilization, cover cropping, and soil tillage.",
  "tutorialControlsPoint3": "Note: Excessive tillage fractures mycorrhizal hyphal networks and over-fertilizing causes nitrate leaching.",
  "tutorialTimelineTitle": "Timeline & Simulation Speed",
  "tutorialTimelineDesc": "Control time progression and observe soil reactions across both diurnal and seasonal cycles.",
  "tutorialTimelinePoint1": "Pause simulation at any moment to thoroughly inspect soil profile state.",
  "tutorialTimelinePoint2": "Adjust simulation speed (1x, 2x, 5x, 10x) to accelerate plant growth and percolation.",
  "tutorialTimelinePoint3": "Scrub the timeline to review earlier days and the impact of weather events.",
  "tutorialObservationTitle": "Observation Modes & Nanovision",
  "tutorialObservationDesc": "Use bottom quick buttons to isolate nutrient cycles and toggle cellular microscopy.",
  "tutorialObservationPoint1": "Nitrogen cycle: Highlight ammonium and nitrate ions along with denitrification gas emissions.",
  "tutorialObservationPoint2": "Nanovision: Inspect stomatal conductance, root apical meristems, and soil pores at up to 1200x magnification.",
  "tutorialObservationPoint3": "Toggle dynamic flow trajectory vectors as needed.",
  "tutorialGamificationTitle": "Sustainability & Objectives",
  "tutorialGamificationDesc": "The top bar measures ecological sustainability and tracks scenario challenges.",
  "tutorialGamificationPoint1": "Monitor soil health index, water saturation, microbial flux, and plant vitality.",
  "tutorialGamificationPoint2": "Achieve scenario objectives (such as carbon sequestration or minimizing leaching) to gain score.",
  "tutorialGamificationPoint3": "Level up by managing the agroecosystem according to sound ecophysiological principles.",
  "quickGuideTabUI": "User Interface",
