  "quickGuideTitle": "SoilScope Quick Guide",
  "stepCompactedClay1Title": "Identify Plow Pan & Compaction",
  "stepCompactedClay1Desc": "Observe soil layers A2 and B1: porosity is critically low and bulk density is elevated (1700-1800 kg/m³). Infiltration is blocked, inhibiting root elongation.",
  "stepCompactedClay2Title": "Soil Loosening & Deep-Rooted Plants",
  "stepCompactedClay2Desc": "Open the right control panel to perform mechanical aeration or subsoiling. Introduce deep-rooted cover crops to forge biopores.",
  "stepCompactedClay3Title": "Monitor Root Penetration",
  "stepCompactedClay3Desc": "Inspect root growth in Nanovision mode. Roots exude organic acids and mucilage (EPS) to stabilize aggregates and enhance hydraulic conductivity.",
  "stepNitrateLeach1Title": "Critical Nitrate Leaching Risk",
  "stepNitrateLeach1Desc": "Topsoil nitrate (NO₃⁻) is dangerously elevated (100 mg/kg) ahead of heavy rainfall. Because nitrate is a mobile anion, it leaches downward with percolating gravitational water.",
  "stepNitrateLeach2Title": "Sow Catch Crops & Regulate Hydrology",
  "stepNitrateLeach2Desc": "Open control panel. Cease fertilization and deploy fast-growing catch crops whose transpiration and uptake sequester free nitrate into biomass.",
  "stepNitrateLeach3Title": "Canopy Nutrient Assimilation",
  "stepNitrateLeach3Desc": "Observe leaf photosynthesis and stomatal conductance. Dense transpiration flux pulls soil solution upward, curtailing deep leaching.",
  "stepNitrogenLock1Title": "Microbial Nitrogen Immobilization (High C/N)",
  "stepNitrogenLock1Desc": "High-carbon straw residue (elevated C:N ratio) stimulates rapid microbial growth, assimilating available mineral nitrogen into biomass and starving the cash crop.",
  "stepNitrogenLock2Title": "Nitrogen Amendment or Legumes",
  "stepNitrogenLock2Desc": "Overcome nitrogen immobilization via targeted mineral N application or by intercropping legumes that fix atmospheric N₂ symbiotically.",
  "stepNitrogenLock3Title": "Observe Remineralization Phase",
  "stepNitrogenLock3Desc": "As microbial biomass turns over, net mineralization resumes. Ammonium and nitrate release into solution, while mineral-associated organic matter (MAOM) stabilizes long-term.",
  "stepWaterlogging1Title": "Waterlogging & Severe Anoxia",
  "stepWaterlogging1Desc": "Water table has reached saturation. Gaseous diffusion ceases, soil dissolved O₂ is consumed, and redox potential (Eh) plunges into reducing anaerobic conditions.",
  "stepWaterlogging2Title": "Root Hypoxia & Wilting",
  "stepWaterlogging2Desc": "Plant roots require O₂ for ATP-driven active nutrient and water uptake. Without aeration, stomata close, and the crop suffers paradoxical wilt despite water excess.",
  "stepWaterlogging3Title": "Improve Drainage & Transpiration",
  "stepWaterlogging3Desc": "Manage water balance: drain excess surface water, stop irrigation, and promote flood-tolerant species featuring internal aerenchyma tissue.",
  "waterloggingTitle": "Waterlogging & Flooding Challenge",
  "waterloggingDesc": "Manage root hypoxia and nutrient dynamics in saturated soil.",
